title Pinewood Derby

participant Arduino
participant Node.js
participant Angular.js
participant Remote Server
participant Mobile Client

note right of Mobile Client:
Creating an event
end note

note right of Node.js:
Emcee runs:
$ node start
end note


Node.js->*Angular.js: xdg-open localhost:8085

Node.js->*Arduino: Open serial port

note right of Angular.js
Emcee creates a new event
end note

Angular.js->Node.js: POST /api/eventNewSave
Node.js->Angular.js: Event created
Angular.js->Remote Server: Replicate database
Mobile Client->Remote Server: GET /api/v3/events
Remote Server->Mobile Client: List of events

note right of Mobile Client:
Checking in a car
end note

Mobile Client->Remote Server: POST /api/v3/checkin
Remote Server->Mobile Client: You are checked in

Angular.js->Remote Server: GET /api/v3/checkinlist
Remote Server->Angular.js: List of checked in cars
note right of Angular.js:
Emcee reviews submission
end note
Angular.js->Node.js: POST /api/newCarSave
Node.js->Angular.js: Car saved
Angular.js->Remote Server: Replicate database
Remote Server-->Mobile Client: socket: New data available
Mobile Client->Remote Server: GET /api/v3/carsAndResultsByEventId?id
Remote Server->Mobile Client: List of cars and results

note right of Mobile Client:
Running a race
end note

note right of Angular.js:
Emcee starts race; the
order of the first eight
cars is determined
end note

note right of Arduino:
Press large red button
end note

Arduino->Node.js: Start
Node.js-->Angular.js: socket: startingGateReleased
note right of Angular.js:
Show live video of race,
begin race timer animation
end note

note right of Angular.js:
Results displayed on screen
as they are received
end note

Arduino->Node.js: Trigger,2,2735634
Node.js-->Angular.js: socket: trigger { 2, 2.735634 }
Angular.js->Node.js: POST /api/result { carId, lane, date, place, time }
Arduino->Node.js: Trigger,3,2965429
Node.js-->Angular.js: socket: trigger { 3, 2.965429 }
Angular.js->Node.js: POST /api/result { carId, lane, date, place, time }
Arduino->Node.js: Trigger,1,3017234
Node.js-->Angular.js: socket: trigger { 1, 3.017234 }
Angular.js->Node.js: POST /api/result { carId, lane, date, place, time }
Arduino->Node.js: Trigger,0,3182639
Node.js-->Angular.js: socket: trigger { 0, 3.182639 }
Angular.js->Node.js: POST /api/result { carId, lane, date, place, time }

note right of Angular.js:
After last result, video is looped
at 0.5x speed and achievements
are calculated
end note

Angular.js->Node.js: POST /api/achievements
Node.js->Angular.js: Saved
Angular.js->Remote Server: Replicate database
Remote Server-->Mobile Client: socket: New data available
Mobile Client->Remote Server: GET /api/v3/carsAndResultsByEventId?id
Remote Server->Mobile Client: List of cars and results

note right of Arduino:
Emcee pushes gate back up
end note
Arduino->Node.js: Ready

Node.js-->Angular.js: socket: readyForStart

note right of Angular.js:
Next four cars are assigned
and displayed on screen
end note